# .env.provider-keys.example - provider API keys, kept in a file SEPARATE from
# the main .env on purpose. Copy to .env.provider-keys and fill in.
#
# Why separate: this file is never CI-bootstrapped (deploy.yml only
# auto-creates <stack_root>/etc/.env from a GitHub secret on first deploy -
# it never touches this one), so an operator creates it manually via SSH and
# can give it stricter host permissions (chmod 400, owner-only) than the
# general operator .env - a smaller blast radius for the one class of secret
# that's runtime-hot (read on every model call) rather than deploy-time.
#
# Legacy path (`config.apiKeyEnvVar` on a model row references one of these
# var names) - TD-006's managed vault (key.provider_api_keys, envelope
# encrypted, configured via capability/provider-keys*) is the target
# state and doesn't need any of these at all. Only fill in what a model row's
# config.apiKeyEnvVar actually references.

DOUBAO_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
